A||||2||Carolina 88GT||Anybody here heavy into amature photography?||||1||
Z||000000||Carolina 88GT||05-19-2000||09:09 PM||||Got a question for you photo gurus out there.  I have a digital camera, complete with tiffen lens adapter so I could attach a 37mm 2x telephoto lens, filters, and wide angle lenses.....I guess my question is, would that 37mm adapter now allow me to use other telephoto lenses/or other types of filters that were only available for traditional 35mm and APS/SLR cameras??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||05-19-2000||11:33 PM||||Hi C88GT,<P>Yes, other filters and lenses will work, with varying levels of success. Filters, especially, will be useful for changes in the basic image, especially a red or green filter if your digicam has a black and white mode. Most diopters (tele, wide angle, fisheye, and closeup converters) will work to a point, and that point is where they vignette, or physically intrude upon the edges of your image.<P>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carolina 88GT||05-20-2000||10:17 AM||||Exactly what I needed to know!  Thanks||||reg||1
